{
    "article_summary": "The article describes the discovery that aryl-substituted ethynylbenziodoxolones (ArEBXs) can be directly activated by visible light irradiation to act as both photooxidants and radical traps. This direct photoexcitation strategy enables decarboxylative, deboronative, and deaminative alkynylations, as well as C-H alkynylation, without the need for an external photocatalyst. Additionally, a photocatalytic method using 4CzIPN was developed to optimize the deoxyalkynylation of tertiary alcohols via oxalate salts, providing access to sterically hindered quaternary centers.",
